{"id": "unknown-2026-10-26-004", "date": "2026-10-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India extends 95% RELIEF export risk cover to March 31, 2027", "content": "India's Department of Commerce has extended RELIEF Component II until March 31, 2027, citing West Asia maritime disruption.\nThe measure offers 95 per cent ECGC risk coverage for eligible Standalone and Whole Turnover Policies obtained on or after March 16, 2026.\nIt covers FCL, LCL and reefer containers, excluding energy shipments; claims are filed through ECGC's customer portal.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-extends-95-relief-export-risk-cover-to-march-31-2027-314535-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-26-005", "date": "2026-10-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["improve", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North India’s cotton yarn market stable, liquidity remains tight", "content": "North India cotton yarn prices stayed stable as weak demand and payment constraints curbed trade in Ludhiana and Delhi; Panipat remained sluggish.\nTraders expect Diwali garment and home textile sales to improve liquidity, restocking and spinning mill cash flow.\nCotton held steady despite weaker ICE trends; mills avoided bulk buying and north India's crop is seen at 26-28 lakh bales.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/north-india-s-cotton-yarn-market-stable-liquidity-remains-tight-314532-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-26-006", "date": "2026-10-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "PTA, polyester melt prices down in India; mixed trend in China", "content": "India’s polyester raw material prices fell further in the October 24 revision, with PTA and polyester melt reduced while MEG stayed unchanged.\nSince October 10, PTA has dropped ₹3.90 (~$0.04) per kg, MEG ₹7 per kg and polyester melt ₹5.74 per kg, extending a domestic correction.\nCFR China PTA rose $25 per tonne during October 19-23, while MEG gained $5 amid Asian petrochemical volatility.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/pta-polyester-melt-prices-down-in-india-mixed-trend-in-china-314524-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-26-007", "date": "2026-10-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India-NZ FTA: Can zero tariffs boost $125.6 mn in textile exports?", "content": "India-New Zealand FTA took effect on October 20, 2026, eliminating duties on all 8,284 New Zealand tariff lines for qualifying Indian goods, including textiles, apparel and carpets.\nSome lines earlier faced tariffs of up to 10 per cent, but benefits depend on HS-code tariffs and rules of origin; TexPro puts New Zealand’s 2025 imports of Indian textiles and apparel at $125.6 million.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-nz-fta-can-zero-tariffs-boost-125-6-mn-in-textile-exports--314517-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
